{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>North.</b> Because he mentioned heaven and earth, and these are two sides, namely above and below, he mentioned north and south. And Tabor is on the west side, and Tabor and Hermon are in the east, and <i>qedem</i> [front/east] is like this and that, just as in the Book of Yetzirah He sealed with six extremities."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {0 "The text reads 'six rings' (שש טבעות), likely referring to the six extremities (שש קצוות) sealed in Sefer Yetzirah; the word טבעות may be a variant reading or scribal corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:28.739167906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}